# Web Quality Gate (Preview & Export)

Scope: **frontend preview and HTML export only**.  
Reference: Modern Web Guidance skill — use for audit guidance, **do not auto-implement** patterns into code.

## Out of scope (do not touch)

- Backend API, services, repositories
- PII pipeline, redaction, privacy storage
- Renderer architecture (`src/rendering/`, section registry, contract adapter)
- Editor UI unless the task explicitly requires it

## After frontend preview/export changes — mandatory checks

**Full pipeline (recommended before handoff / demo):**

```powershell
cd C:\Dima\Projects\CURSOR\Lend
.\scripts\check_all.ps1 -ProjectId {id}
```

Requires backend + frontend running for smoke steps. Log: `logs/qa/check_all_*.log`

**Minimum if check_all is too slow:**

Run in order:

1. `cd frontend && npm test`
2. `cd frontend && npm run build`
3. Manual review: `http://localhost:3000/preview/{id}?style=university_platform`
4. DevTools Console — **zero errors** (including hydration warnings)
5. `cd backend && ..\.venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts\smoke_university_export.py --project-id {id}`
6. `cd frontend && node scripts/smoke-visual-acceptance.mjs --project-id {id}`

Full checklist: `docs/WEB_QUALITY_GATE.md`  
Visual acceptance (university_platform): `frontend/docs/VISUAL_ACCEPTANCE_UNIVERSITY.md`  
One-command QA: `README_RUN.md` → One-command QA pipeline

## Style constraints — `university_platform`

- Light academic palette; readable typography
- **Forbidden**: random gradients, dark theme, glassmorphism, neon/decorative effects
- Do not rewrite working preview/export code without an explicit task

## Dependencies

- Do **not** add new npm libraries without justification in the task
- Prefer existing tokens, Tailwind utilities, and StyleProfile CSS vars

## Audit areas (reference Modern Web Guidance when reviewing)

Responsive 360/768/1440 · heading hierarchy · aria-labels · keyboard nav · contrast · no console/hydration errors · no heavy animations · export opens standalone
